# An [[incidental]] remark; especially {{context|legal|lang=en}} a statement or remark in a court's [[judgment]] that is not essential to the [[disposition]] of the case. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
#*'''1971''', {{w|Keith Thomas (historian)|Keith Thomas}}, ''Religion and the Decline of Magic'', Folio Society 2012, p. 128:
#*:Casual '''''obiter dicta''''' by men of accepted godliness belonged to a different category from the ecstatic claims to immediate revelation made by obscure persons who thrust themselves into the limelight […].

